{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type MergeContextForJoinCallback<TContext, TNewSchema> = Omit<TContext, \"schema\" | \"refsSchema\" | \"hasJoins\" | \"joinTypes\"> & object;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L1328","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:1328"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MergeContextForJoinCallback - Special context for join condition callbacks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This type creates a context specifically for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCallback"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter of join operations.\nThe key difference from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MergeContextWithJoinType"},{"type":"text","value":" is that NO optionality is applied here."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why No Optionality?"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nIn SQL, join conditions are evaluated BEFORE optionality is determined. Both tables\nmust be treated as available (non-optional) within the join condition itself.\nOptionality is only applied to the result AFTER the join logic executes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":".from({ users })\n.leftJoin({ orders }, ({ users, orders }) => {\n  // users is NOT optional here - we can access users.id directly\n  // orders is NOT optional here - we can access orders.userId directly\n  return eq(users.id, orders.userId)\n})\n.where(({ orders }) => {\n  // NOW orders is optional because it's after the LEFT JOIN\n  return orders?.status === 'pending'\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The simple intersection (&) merges schemas without any optionality transformation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-declaration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Declaration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"baseschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"baseSchema"}]},{"type":"code","value":"baseSchema: TContext[\"baseSchema\"];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fromsourcename","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fromSourceName"}]},{"type":"code","value":"fromSourceName: TContext[\"fromSourceName\"];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hasjoins","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hasJoins"}]},{"type":"code","value":"hasJoins: true;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"jointypes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"joinTypes"}]},{"type":"code","value":"joinTypes: TContext[\"joinTypes\"] extends Record<string, any> ? TContext[\"joinTypes\"] : object & { [K in keyof TNewSchema & string]: \"inner\" };","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"refsschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"refsSchema"}]},{"type":"code","value":"refsSchema: RefsSchemaForContext<TContext> & TNewSchema;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"schema"}]},{"type":"code","value":"schema: TContext[\"schema\"] & TNewSchema;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tcontext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TContext"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/Context.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Context"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tnewschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TNewSchema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TNewSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"ContextSchema.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ContextSchema"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-declaration","text":"Type Declaration","level":2},{"id":"baseschema","text":"baseSchema","level":3},{"id":"fromsourcename","text":"fromSourceName","level":3},{"id":"hasjoins","text":"hasJoins","level":3},{"id":"jointypes","text":"joinTypes","level":3},{"id":"refsschema","text":"refsSchema","level":3},{"id":"schema","text":"schema","level":3},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tcontext","text":"TContext","level":3},{"id":"tnewschema","text":"TNewSchema","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype MergeContextForJoinCallback<TContext, TNewSchema> = Omit<TContext, \"schema\" | \"refsSchema\" | \"hasJoins\" | \"joinTypes\"> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:1328](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L1328)\n\nMergeContextForJoinCallback - Special context for join condition callbacks\n\nThis type creates a context specifically for the `onCallback` parameter of join operations.\nThe key difference from `MergeContextWithJoinType` is that NO optionality is applied here.\n\n**Why No Optionality?**\nIn SQL, join conditions are evaluated BEFORE optionality is determined. Both tables\nmust be treated as available (non-optional) within the join condition itself.\nOptionality is only applied to the result AFTER the join logic executes.\n\n**Example**:\n```typescript\n.from({ users })\n.leftJoin({ orders }, ({ users, orders }) => {\n  // users is NOT optional here - we can access users.id directly\n  // orders is NOT optional here - we can access orders.userId directly\n  return eq(users.id, orders.userId)\n})\n.where(({ orders }) => {\n  // NOW orders is optional because it's after the LEFT JOIN\n  return orders?.status === 'pending'\n})\n```\n\nThe simple intersection (&) merges schemas without any optionality transformation.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### baseSchema\n\n```ts\nbaseSchema: TContext[\"baseSchema\"];\n```\n\n### fromSourceName\n\n```ts\nfromSourceName: TContext[\"fromSourceName\"];\n```\n\n### hasJoins\n\n```ts\nhasJoins: true;\n```\n\n### joinTypes\n\n```ts\njoinTypes: TContext[\"joinTypes\"] extends Record<string, any> ? TContext[\"joinTypes\"] : object & { [K in keyof TNewSchema & string]: \"inner\" };\n```\n\n### refsSchema\n\n```ts\nrefsSchema: RefsSchemaForContext<TContext> & TNewSchema;\n```\n\n### schema\n\n```ts\nschema: TContext[\"schema\"] & TNewSchema;\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` *extends* [`Context`](../interfaces/Context.md)\n\n### TNewSchema\n\n`TNewSchema` *extends* [`ContextSchema`](ContextSchema.md)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: MergeContextForJoinCallback\ntitle: MergeContextForJoinCallback\n---\n\n```ts\ntype MergeContextForJoinCallback<TContext, TNewSchema> = Omit<TContext, \"schema\" | \"refsSchema\" | \"hasJoins\" | \"joinTypes\"> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:1328](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L1328)\n\nMergeContextForJoinCallback - Special context for join condition callbacks\n\nThis type creates a context specifically for the `onCallback` parameter of join operations.\nThe key difference from `MergeContextWithJoinType` is that NO optionality is applied here.\n\n**Why No Optionality?**\nIn SQL, join conditions are evaluated BEFORE optionality is determined. Both tables\nmust be treated as available (non-optional) within the join condition itself.\nOptionality is only applied to the result AFTER the join logic executes.\n\n**Example**:\n```typescript\n.from({ users })\n.leftJoin({ orders }, ({ users, orders }) => {\n  // users is NOT optional here - we can access users.id directly\n  // orders is NOT optional here - we can access orders.userId directly\n  return eq(users.id, orders.userId)\n})\n.where(({ orders }) => {\n  // NOW orders is optional because it's after the LEFT JOIN\n  return orders?.status === 'pending'\n})\n```\n\nThe simple intersection (&) merges schemas without any optionality transformation.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### baseSchema\n\n```ts\nbaseSchema: TContext[\"baseSchema\"];\n```\n\n### fromSourceName\n\n```ts\nfromSourceName: TContext[\"fromSourceName\"];\n```\n\n### hasJoins\n\n```ts\nhasJoins: true;\n```\n\n### joinTypes\n\n```ts\njoinTypes: TContext[\"joinTypes\"] extends Record<string, any> ? TContext[\"joinTypes\"] : object & { [K in keyof TNewSchema & string]: \"inner\" };\n```\n\n### refsSchema\n\n```ts\nrefsSchema: RefsSchemaForContext<TContext> & TNewSchema;\n```\n\n### schema\n\n```ts\nschema: TContext[\"schema\"] & TNewSchema;\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` *extends* [`Context`](../interfaces/Context.md)\n\n### TNewSchema\n\n`TNewSchema` *extends* [`ContextSchema`](ContextSchema.md)\n"}
